   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.1. Increased institutional capacity of employer and business membership organizations (EBMOs)</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Employers Federation of Pakistan (EFP) has actively delivered training across various disciplines on capacity building of professionals within the corporate sector. Originally conducted in face-to-face formats, these training programmes underwent a shift towards online and hybrid setups (combining physical and online formats) due to COVID-19. 
Responding to its desire to augment its training, EFP established an E-learning platform. EFP launched its inaugural course on E-learning platform titled &#x201C;WE &#x2013; RISE&#x201D; (Women Empowerment Rise in July 2023 with 32 enterprises. EFP further announced its second course, &#x201C;Key Compliance Challenges and Solutions on Sindh Labour laws&#x201D;. In addition, the EFP Focal point for the E-learning platform designed a youth-oriented course titled &#x201C;EFP Future Fit Course for Youth&#x201D;.
One of the prevailing challenges of Pakistan pertains to labour law compliance. In response, EFP adapted the ILO COMPLIANCE+tool, originally introduced in Sri Lanka in 2014. This localized version of the tool enhanced EFP&#x2019;s existing enterprise auditing tool and methodology with aims to bolster business members&#x2019; compliance to fundamental labour standards. Eight EFP trainers are well-equipped to offer further support using the ILO SCORE Lean methodology to assist EFP members in their endeavours. 
Making use of the ILO COMPLIANCE + tool, EFP conducted a series of awareness-raising events on Occupational Safety and Health (OSH) Convention No. 155 and 187 between February  - April 2023. Furthermore, EFP provided capacity building trainings to employers&#x2019; representatives and enterprises regarding the Generalized System of Preference Plus (GSP+) and its linkage with ILS. 85 employer representatives have been trained so far.
The establishment of the e-learning platform, the implementation of the Compliance+ tool, and the conducted training have collectively enriched EFP&apos;s portfolio of training services, enhancing its overall service offering. ILO collaborated with ITC to support EFP to establish the E-learning platform. Initially, three EFP officials received training from ITC-ILO on effectively utilizing the platform for training purposes. These officials participated in a 7-week online E-design training programme offered by ITC-ILO in 2022.
The ILO initiated the process by delivering an introductory presentation to EFP on the Sri Lankan case study of COMPLIANCE +. During this discussion, ILO delineated how EFP should tailor the tool to align with its specific requirements.
For the adaptation and localization of the COMPLIANCE+tool, the ILO with EU funding played a supportive role in reviewing the national labour legislation. Furthermore, ILO facilitated a series of capacity-building sessions and consultations on GSP+ and the alignment with international labour standards.</narrative>
   </description>
